# SQL migration files must be byte-identical on every checkout platform:
# their SHA256 checksum is load-bearing (docs/design/03-v1-alpha-foundation.md
# V1-04's tamper detection — internal/adapters/sqlite/migrations.go computes
# it from the embedded file bytes). Line-ending normalization on checkout
# would silently change that checksum per-platform, so it must never apply
# here regardless of a contributor's or CI runner's core.autocrlf setting.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Golden JSON fixtures (e.g. internal/app/doctor/testdata/golden/*.json)
# are compared byte-for-byte against freshly json.MarshalIndent-ed output,
# which always emits LF only. Without this, a Windows checkout normalizes
# these to CRLF while Linux keeps LF, making the exact same golden test
# pass on one CI OS and fail on the other for a reason that has nothing to
# do with the code under test (V1-11 hit this for real on windows-latest —
# same root cause as the *.sql rule above).
*.json text eol=lf
